// #taxon[Taxon]
#title[Dirichlet Series]

Given a species $F$ we obtain a dirichlet series $hat(F)$, classically given by
$
  hat(F) (s) := sum_(n >= 1) (|F(n)|)/(n!) n^(-s).
$
See #local("00DU")[the paper].
A categorification of this is the $H$-Dirichlet series in #local("00B8")[agda-unimath] defined for $H : Uu ->
Uu$ with $H(X xx Y) ~= H(X) xx H(Y)$ by
$
  Sigma (X : "FinSet"), (F(X) × (S → H(X))).
$
Evidentily this is a good definition to recover a lot of algebraic properties
of the dirichlet product, as has been done in agda unimath.

For $X : "FinSet"$, consider $H(X) :-= B C_n$, where $n$ is the cardinality of $X$, and $B C_n$ the delooping of the cyclic group in $n$ elements. Then this could be a nice categorification of the dirichlet series, since the #local("007P")[groupoid cardinality] of $B C_n$ is
$
  |B C_n| = 1/n .. "and" .. |S -> B C_n| = n^(-|S|)
$

Note though that $H$ is not multiplicative in the sense of the $H$-Dirichlet series. E.g.
$
  "TODO"
$

But we still get multiplicativity of cardinalities (hopefully), since
$
  |B C_n| |B C_m|= 1/n * 1/m = 1/(n m) = |B C_(n m)|
$

Define the categorified version of the dirichlet series to be
$
  Dd_F (S) :-= sum  (X : "FinSet"), (F(X) × (S → B C_(|X|)))
$
the we can decategorigy by taking the groupoid cardinality (in the case where F is wellbehaved)
TODO : elaborate on constraints
$
  hat(F) (s) &:= |Dd_F ([s])|\
  &= |sum  (X : "FinSet"), (F(X) × ([s] → B C_(|X|)))| \
  &= sum_(n >= 1) (|F([n])|)/(n!) * n^(-s)
$

-> Still need to work out how to take the groupoidcardinality in HoTT and in which cases this is well-defined.

